 "title": "44: LFH Overflow",
 "desc": "LFH heap overflow — chunk A is adjacent to chunk B which contains a function pointer. Overflow A's data into B to overwrite the function pointer with win(). Despite LFH randomization, heap spraying makes adjacent placement likely.",
 "mode": "heap-overflow",
